Disable compiler options

The project adds -Werror options with add_compile_options(), which are placed
after CXXFLAGS on the compiler command line, so they cannot be turned off with
-Wno-error=... from the recipe. They break the build with the toolchain GCC:
exceptions.hpp:71:79: error: declaration of 'invalid_index' shadows a member of 'rclcpp::exceptions::InvalidNodeNameError' [-Werror=shadow]

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5.5
AI-Generated: Uses Claude (claude-sonnet-5.5)
Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,8 +2,6 @@
 project(control_toolbox LANGUAGES CXX)
 
 if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "(GNU|Clang)")
-  add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror=conversion -Werror=unused-but-set-variable
-                      -Werror=return-type -Werror=shadow -Werror=format)
 endif()
 
 if(WIN32)
